97", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D001943", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D001943"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D001943", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Breast Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Breast_Neoplasms"}, "text": "BC", "locations": [{"offset": 25404, "length": 2}]}, {"id": "38298", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D010051", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D010051"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D010051", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Ovarian Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Ovarian_Neoplasms"}, "text": "OC", "locations": [{"offset": 25684, "length": 2}]}, {"id": "38299", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "women", "locations": [{"offset": 25393, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "38300", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D001943", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D001943"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D001943", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Breast Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Breast_Neoplasms"}, "text": "BC", "locations": [{"offset": 25823, "length": 2}]}, {"id": "38301", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D001943", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D001943"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D001943", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Breast Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Breast_Neoplasms"}, "text": "BC", "locations": [{"offset": 25131, "length": 2}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "RESULTS", "type": "title_2"}, "offset": 26445, "text": "3.7. Genotype-Phenotype Correlations", "sentences": [], "annotations": [], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "RESULTS", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 26482, "text": "For each subgroup of the cohort (female BC, male BC, OC, other cancers, and/or positive familiarity), clinical features were first compared between LP/P variants carriers (P/LP patients) and probands with not informative tests (NI, that is patients with VUS, B/LB, or no variants), then between P/LP patients and each of the two NI subclasses: negative (N, that is patients with B/LB or no variants) and VUS, and finally, between the latter two (Tables S4-S7)", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "38302", "infons": {"identifier": "5744", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "2113", "valid": true, "normalized": [5744], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 5744, "biotype": "gene", "name": "PTHLH", "accession": "@GENE_PTHLH"}, "text": "P/LP", "locations": [{"offset": 26777, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "38303", "infons": {"identifier": "5744", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "2113", "valid": true, "normalized": [5744], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 5744, "biotype": "gene", "name": "PTHLH", "accession": "@GENE_PTHLH"}, "text": "P/LP", "locations": [{"offset": 26654, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "38304", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D009369", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D009369"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D009369", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Neoplasms"}, "text": "cancers", "locations": [{"offset": 26545, "length": 7}]}, {"id": "38305", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D001943", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D001943"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D001943", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Breast Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Breast_Neoplasms"}, "text": "BC", "locations": [{"offset": 26522, "length": 2}]}, {"id": "38306", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "patients", "locations": [{"offset": 26847, "length": 8}]}, {"id": "38307", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:C537419", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["C537419"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "C537419", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Bohring syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Bohring_syndrome"}, "text": "LB", "locations": [{"offset": 26863, "length": 2}]}, {"id": "38308", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "patients", "locations": [{"offset": 26782, "length": 8}]}, {"id": "38309", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:C537419", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["C537419"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "C537419", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Bohring syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Bohring_syndrome"}, "text": "LB", "locations": [{"offset": 26743, "length": 2}]}, {"id": "38310", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D065309", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D065309"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D065309", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Atypical Squamous Cells of the Cervix", "accession": "@DISEASE_Atypical_Squamous_Cells_of_the_Cervix"}, "text": "VUS", "locations": [{"offset": 26736, "length": 3}]}, {"id": "38311", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "patients", "locations": [{"offset": 26659, "length": 8}]}, {"id": "38312", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D010051", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D010051"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D010051", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Ovarian Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Ovarian_Neoplasms"}, "text": "OC", "locations": [{"offset": 26535, "length": 2}]}, {"id": "38313", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:C537419", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["C537419"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "C537419", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Bohring syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Bohring_syndrome"}, "text": "LP", "locations": [{"offset": 26630, "length": 2}]}, {"id": "38314", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "patients", "locations": [{"offset": 26722, "length": 8}]}, {"id": "38316", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D065309", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D065309"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D065309", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Atypical Squamous Cells of the Cervix", "accession": "@DISEASE_Atypical_Squamous_Cells_of_the_Cervix"}, "text": "VUS", "locations": [{"offset": 26886, "length": 3}]}, {"id": "38318", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D001943", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D001943"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D001943", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Breast Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Breast_Neoplasms"}, "text": "BC", "locations": [{"offset": 26531, "length": 2}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "RESULTS", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 26944, "text": "Compared to NI-fBC and its subclasses, in P/LP-fBC patients, a bilateral disease was significantly more frequent. Hormone responsive and Her2 (Human epidermal growth factor receptor 2) positive phenotype was rarer in P/LP BC cases and significantly higher in NI ones. In addition, familiarity for BC was less recurrent among relatives of P/LP women compared to NI, N, and VUS cases, but splitting up first and second-degree kinds, this difference remained significant only in the latter. Conversely, although not statistically significant, a trend of higher PrC familiarity emerged among P/LP-fBC first-degree relatives. No other differences were found in other demographic, clinical, and familial features (Table S4). Among OC patients, P/LP OC was younger than NI, N, and VUS OC cases, and, in their families, BC and PrC recurred more frequently in the first degree and second-degree relatives, respectively (Table S5). No differences emerged comparing mBC with and without P/LP variants (Table S6), while, among cases with other cancers and/or malignancies in relatives, P/LP variants were detected exclusively in affected probands rather than in healthy ones (Table S7).", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "38319", "infons": {"identifier": "2064", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "3273", "valid": true, "normalized": [2064], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 2064, "biotype": "gene", "name": "ERBB2", "accession": "@GENE_ERBB2"}, "text": "Her2", "locations": [{"offset": 27081, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "38320", "infons": {"identifier": "2064", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "3273", "valid": true, "normalized": [2064], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 2064, "biotype": "gene", "name": "ERBB2", "accession": "@GENE_ERBB2"}, "text": "Human epidermal growth factor receptor 2", "locations": [{"offset": 27087, "length": 40}]}, {"id": "38321", "infons": {"identifier": "5744", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "2113", "valid": true, "normalized": [5744], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 5744, "biotype": "gene", "name": "PTHLH", "accession": "@GENE_PTHLH"}, "text": "P/LP", "locations": [{"offset": 28018, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "38322", "infons": {"identifier": "5744", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "2113", "valid": true, "normalized": [5744], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 5744, "biotype": "gene", "name": "PTHLH", "accession": "@GENE_PTHLH"}, "text": "P/LP", "locations": [{"offset": 27920, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "38323", "infons": {"identifier": "5744", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "2113", "valid": true, "normalized": [5744], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 5744, "biotype": "gene", "name": "PTHLH", "accession": "@GENE_PTHLH"}, "text": "P/LP", "locations": [{"offset": 27682, "length": 4}]}, {"id":