, "name": "c.363_364del", "accession": "@VARIANT_c.363_364del_RECQL_human"}, "text": "c.363_364del", "locations": [{"offset": 37202, "length": 12}]}, {"id": "38588", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D009369", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D009369"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D009369", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Neoplasms"}, "text": "cancer", "locations": [{"offset": 37520, "length": 6}]}, {"id": "38589", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D014898", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D014898"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D014898", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Werner Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Werner_Syndrome"}, "text": "Werner Syndrome", "locations": [{"offset": 37568, "length": 15}]}, {"id": "38590", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D043171", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D043171"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D043171", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Chromosomal Instability", "accession": "@DISEASE_Chromosomal_Instability"}, "text": "chromosomal instability", "locations": [{"offset": 37938, "length": 23}]}, {"id": "38591", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D011038", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D011038"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D011038", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Rothmund-Thomson Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Rothmund_Thomson_Syndrome"}, "text": "Rothmund-Thomson Syndrome", "locations": [{"offset": 37589, "length": 25}]}, {"id": "38592", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D001943", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D001943"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D001943", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Breast Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Breast_Neoplasms"}, "text": "BC", "locations": [{"offset": 38372, "length": 2}]}, {"id": "38593", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D001816", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D001816"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D001816", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Bloom Syndrome", "accession": "@DISEASE_Bloom_Syndrome"}, "text": "Bloom Syndrome", "locations": [{"offset": 37552, "length": 14}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "DISCUSS", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 38730, "text": "More than 20% of patients have carried VUS. This type of inconclusive result is a hard challenge to face. With the advent of panel analysis, the number of VUS has increased exponentially, and still, too often, their interpretation remains tangled and blurred. Unfortunately, in most cases, VUS causes difficulty in risk assessment, sometimes overtreatment, and usually anxiety in carriers. Bioinformatic analysis, functional studies, and periodical updates performed by international consortia are the currently available strategies to shed light on this issue.", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "38594", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D065309", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D065309"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D065309", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Atypical Squamous Cells of the Cervix", "accession": "@DISEASE_Atypical_Squamous_Cells_of_the_Cervix"}, "text": "VUS", "locations": [{"offset": 39020, "length": 3}]}, {"id": "38595", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D065309", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D065309"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D065309", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Atypical Squamous Cells of the Cervix", "accession": "@DISEASE_Atypical_Squamous_Cells_of_the_Cervix"}, "text": "VUS", "locations": [{"offset": 38769, "length": 3}]}, {"id": "38596", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "patients", "locations": [{"offset": 38747, "length": 8}]}, {"id": "38597", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D001007", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D001007"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D001007", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Anxiety", "accession": "@DISEASE_Anxiety"}, "text": "anxiety", "locations": [{"offset": 39099, "length": 7}]}, {"id": "38598", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D065309", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D065309"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D065309", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Atypical Squamous Cells of the Cervix", "accession": "@DISEASE_Atypical_Squamous_Cells_of_the_Cervix"}, "text": "VUS", "locations": [{"offset": 38885, "length": 3}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "DISCUSS", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 39292, "text": "Laboratories and clinicians should collaborate in order to guarantee periodical re-evaluations and updates on their variants to VUS carriers.", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "38599", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D065309", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D065309"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D065309", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Atypical Squamous Cells of the Cervix", "accession": "@DISEASE_Atypical_Squamous_Cells_of_the_Cervix"}, "text": "VUS", "locations": [{"offset": 39420, "length": 3}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "DISCUSS", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 39434, "text": "The comparison of clinical and familial features between patients with and without P/LP variants brought out interesting suggestions. In our cohort, P/LP variants were more frequent in women with bilateral BC, as reported before. There was not a prevalent histological phenotype in mutated BC women compared to BC cases without damaging mutation nor a strong recurrence of specific types of cancers among relatives. Intriguingly, but not surprisingly, a trend of higher frequency of prostatic cancer among relatives of BC women with P/LP variants emerged. This association was stronger in relatives of mutated OC patients. Pathogenic variants in DDR and MMR genes, usually analyzed in suspected hereditary BC and OC, have been recently associated also with hereditary prostatic cancer.", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "38600", "infons": {"identifier": "5744", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "2113", "valid": true, "normalized": [5744], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 5744, "biotype": "gene", "name": "PTHLH", "accession": "@GENE_PTHLH"}, "text": "P/LP", "locations": [{"offset": 39517, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "38601", "infons": {"identifier": "5744", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "2113", "valid": true, "normalized": [5744], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 5744, "biotype": "gene", "name": "PTHLH", "accession": "@GENE_PTHLH"}, "text": "P/LP", "locations": [{"offset": 39583, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "38602", "infons": {"identifier": "5744", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "2113", "valid": true, "normalized": [5744], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 5744, "biotype": "gene", "name": "PTHLH", "accession": "@GENE_PTHLH"}, "text": "P/LP", "locations": [{"offset": 39967, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "38603", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D011471", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D011471"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D011471", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Prostatic Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Prostatic_Neoplasms"}, "text": "prostatic cancer", "locations": [{"offset": 39917, "length": 16}]}, {"id": "38604", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D001943", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D001943"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D001943", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Breast Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Breast_Neoplasms"}, "text": "BC", "locations": [{"offset": 39724, "length": 2}]}, {"id": "38605", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:C537243", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["C537243"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "C537243", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Prostate cancer familial", "accession": "@DISEASE_Prostate_cancer_familial"}, "text": "hereditary prostatic cancer", "locations": [{"offset": 40191, "length": 27}]}, {"id": "38606", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D010051", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D010051"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D010051", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Ovarian Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Ovarian_Neoplasms"}, "text": "OC", "locations": [{"offset": 40147, "length": 2}]}, {"id": "38607", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "women", "locations": [{"offset": 39956, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "38608", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "women", "locations": [{"offset": 39727, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "38609", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "patients", "locations": [{"offset": 40047, "length": 8}]}, {"id": "38610", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D001943", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D001943"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D001943", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Breast Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Breast_Neoplasms"}, "text": "BC", "locations": [{"offset": 40140, "length": 2}]}, {"id": "38611", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "patients", "locations": [{"offset": 39491, "length": 8}]}, {"id": "38612", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "women", "locations": [{"offset": 39619, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "38613", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D001943", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D001943"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D001943", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Breast Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Breast_Neoplasms"}, "text": "BC", "locations": [{"offset": 39640, "length": 2}]}, {"id": "38614", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D001943", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D001943"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D001943", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Breast Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Breast_Neoplasms"}, "text": "BC", "locations": [{"offset": 39745, "length": 2}]}, {"id": "38615", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D001943", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D001943"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D001943", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Breast Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Breast_Neoplasms"}, "text": "BC", "locations": [{"offset": 39953, "length": 2}]}, {"id": "38616", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D009369", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D009369"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D009369", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Neoplasms"}, "text": "cancers", "locations": [{"offset": 39825, "length": 7}]}, {"id": "38617", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D010051", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D010051"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D010051", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Ovarian Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Ovarian_Neoplasms"}, "text": "OC", "locations": [{"offset": 40044, "length": 2}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "DISCUSS", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 40220, "text": "A wider number of probands and the availability of segregation among relatives would have given the opportunity to furtherly strengthen the association between the identified variants and the predisposition to cancer. Future studies investigating P/LP variants in DDR genes in many BC, OC, and PC cases, familial or sporadic, and in their relatives would be necessary to better define the role and the weight of these genes in determining malignancies.", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "38618", "infons": {"identifier": "5744", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "2113", "valid": true, "normalized": [5744], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 5744, "biotype": "gene", "name": "PTHLH", "accession": "@GENE_PTHLH"}, "text": "P/LP", "locations": [{"offset": 40467, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "38619", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D001943", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D001943"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D001943", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Breast Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Breast_Neoplasms"}, "text": "BC", "locations": [{"offset": 40502, "length": 2}]}, {"id": "38621", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D009369", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D009369"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D009369", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Neoplasms"}, "text": "malignancies", "locations": [{"offset": 40659, "length": 12}]}, {"id": "38622", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D010195", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D010195"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D010195", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Pancreatitis", "accession": "@DISEASE_Pancreatitis"}, "text": "PC", "locations": [{"offset": 40514, "length": 2}]}, {"id": "38623", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D009369", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D009369"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D009369", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Neoplasms"}, "text": "cancer", "locations": [{"offset": 40430, "length": 6}]}, {"id": "38624", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D010051", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D010051"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D010051", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Ovarian Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Ovarian_Neoplasms"}, "text": "OC", "locations": [{"offset": 40506, "length": 2}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "DISCUSS", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 40673, "text": "In conclusion, in this study, we described that 14% of non-BRCA patients with BC/OC tumors are carriers of pathogenic variants in other genes, particularly CHEK2, RAD51C, ATM, MLH1, MSH2, RECQL, all related with the BRCA1/2 DNA repair pathway. This result shows that the DDR genes panel significantly increases the diagnostic power in patients with personal and/or family history of breast/ovarian and pancreatic cancers.", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "38625", "infons": {"identifier": "672", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "5276", "valid": true, "normalized": [672], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 672, "biotype": "gene", "name": "BRCA1", "accession": "@GENE_BRCA1"}, "text": "BRCA", "locations": [{"offset": 40732, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "38626", "infons": {"identifier": "11200", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "38289", "valid": true, "normalized": [11200], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 11200, "biotype": "gene", "name": "CHEK2", "accession": "@GENE_CHEK2"}, "text": "CHEK2", "locations": [{"offset": 40829, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "38627", "infons": {"identifier": "5889", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "14238", "valid": true, "normalized": [5889], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 5889, "biotype": "gene", "name": "RAD51C", "accession": "@GENE_RAD51C"}, "text": "RAD51C", "locations": [{"offset": 40836, "length": 6}]}, {"id": "38628", "infons": {"identifier": "472", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "30952", "valid": true, "normalized": [472], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 472, "biotype": "gene", "name": "ATM", "accession": "@GENE_ATM"}, "text": "ATM", "locations": [{"offset": 40844, "length": 3}]}, {"id": "38629", "infons": {"identifier": "4292", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "208", "valid": true, "normalized": [4292], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 4292, "biotype": "gene", "name": "MLH1", "accession": "@GENE_MLH1"}, "text": "MLH1", "locations": [{"offset": 40849, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "38630", "infons": {"identifier": "4436", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "210", "valid": true, "normalized": [4436], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 4436, "biotype": "gene", "name": "MSH2", "accession": "@GENE_MSH2"}, "text": "MSH2", "locations": [{"offset": 40855, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "38631", "infons": {"identifier": "5965", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "56279", "valid": true, "normalized": [5965], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 5965, "biotype": "gene", "name": "RECQL", "accession": "@GENE_RECQL"}, "text": "RECQL", "locations": [{"offset": 40861, "length": 5}]}, {"id": "38632", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "patients", "locations": [{"offset": 40737, "length": 8}]}, {"id": "38633", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D001943", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D001943"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D001943", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Breast Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Breast_Neoplasms"}, "text": "BC/OC tumors", "locations": [{"offset": 40751, "length": 12}]}, {"id": "38634", "infons": {"identifier": "9606", "type": "Species", "valid": true, "normalized": [9606], "database": "ncbi_taxonomy", "normalized_id": 9606, "biotype": "species", "name": "9606", "accession": null}, "text": "patients", "locations": [{"offset": 41008, "length": 8}]}, {"id": "38635", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D010051", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D010051"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D010051", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Ovarian Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Ovarian_Neoplasms"}, "text": "breast/ovarian and pancreatic cancers", "locations": [{"offset": 41056, "length": 37}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "DISCUSS", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 41095, "text": "The identification of mutations in genes involved in DNA damage response, other than BRCA, explains the strong tumor recurrence in some families and may contribute to the development of new and more specific clinical management programs and pave the way to new therapeutic opportunities.", "sentences": [], "annotations": [{"id": "38636", "infons": {"identifier": "672", "type": "Gene", "ncbi_homologene": "5276", "valid": true, "normalized": [672], "database": "ncbi_gene", "normalized_id": 672, "biotype": "gene", "name": "BRCA1", "accession": "@GENE_BRCA1"}, "text": "BRCA", "locations": [{"offset": 41180, "length": 4}]}, {"id": "38637", "infons": {"identifier": "MESH:D009369", "type": "Disease", "valid": true, "normalized": ["D009369"], "database": "ncbi_mesh", "normalized_id": "D009369", "biotype": "disease", "name": "Neoplasms", "accession": "@DISEASE_Neoplasms"}, "text": "tumor", "locations": [{"offset": 41206, "length": 5}]}], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "SUPPL", "type": "title"}, "offset": 41383, "text": "Supplementary Materials", "sentences": [], "annotations": [], "relations": []}, {"infons": {"section_type": "SUPPL", "type": "paragraph"}, "offset": 41407, "text": "The following are available online at , Figure S1: Pedigrees of five families with P/LP variants, Figure S2: Pedigrees of CHEK2 families. Individuals with any cancer are shown as filled circles, Table S1: Design of multigene panel, Table S2: Sequencing metrics by NGS Analysis, Table S3: Clinical characteristics of probands with VUS variants, Table S4: Females with breast cancer (fBC),